  "body": "**Problem.** The PR for #3919 (first slice) adds these tapers to the built-in holder library: `HSK-A63`, `HSK-F63`, `HSK-E40`, `HSK-E32`, `SK30`, `SK40` and `ISO30`. A machine file can not state them yet. `camcraft_post::machine::SPINDLE_MOUNTS` (`crates/post/src/machine/tooling.rs`) holds only `BT30`, `BT40`, `CAT40` and `TTS`. A `.mch` with `\"spindle_mount\": \"HSK-A63\"` is refused with \"is not a spindle mount the holder library knows\".\n\n**Found while** working #3919. The library slice keeps the machine-file rule as it is, so that the slice stays in the tools crate.\n\n**Do:**\n- Add the new taper names to `SPINDLE_MOUNTS`, or read the list from the holder library through the lookup that the caller passes in already (`HolderLookup`).\n- Update the tests that use a mount name as the \"unknown\" example, if a new name makes them pass by accident.\n\n**Done means:** a machine file that states one of the new tapers loads, its `default_holder` must sit in that taper, and a pinning test covers one HSK and one SK mount.\n",
